								<a href="mailto:Ssnakess@mail2hell.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=805.msg8155#msg8155"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=805.msg8155#msg8155">Re: Perfect Group</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #17 on:</b> June 01, 2004, 04:08:38 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							My &quot;perfect&quot; group would have to be..<br /><br />Cleric, Shaman, Paladin, Monk, Enchanter, Druid.<br /><br />Paladin because they can tank most anything, and backup rez/heals.<br /><br />Monk because we&#039;re not afraid to do crazy shit that no one else will try and the years of pulling experience kinda pay off in unknown places....plus it wouldn&#039;t be my perfect group if I wasn&#039;t included, now would it?<br /><br />Druid for tracking, snares, back up heals, etc.<br /><br />Cleric, shaman, and enchanter for obvious reasons.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
